Z||000000||Coupe'N||07-02-2001||11:26 PM||||I was looking in the archives and it seems as if Fierocious and kidzwheelz got pretty darn far on this turbo duke set up. WHAT HAPPENED???? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001019-2-002293.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001019-2-002293.html</A> <BR> Anyone know? Just wondering!<P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||FIEROCIOUS||09-12-2001||01:09 PM||||Wow, haven't been here in a while!<P>All that was done was pretty much written in the posts in that thread.<BR>The only things me and Kidz did in addition to is he bought a holley Throttle Body and a K&N top that sealed the TB. That was the missing part we needed to seal the turbo to the TB. All that remained (past tense) was to fabricate the exhaust and intake to connect it all together. <BR>After talking to several people who do this kind of stuff daily, both me and Kidz were confident it would work either way, Quad 4 ECM or riseing rate fuel regulator and even the combination of both (recomended). Kidz has since sold the Fiero and I have seen it on the roads running. I have no clue if the owner finished what we started or not? Kidz had to sell it due to sepperation and a transfer to Virginia were he now lives.<P>If you have any questions, I'd be happy to help if I can.<p>[This message has been edited by FIEROCIOUS (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||12
